        "findings": [
          "The theme has no variable for direction, language or script, and none for font family (fonts are left to the app; Tailwind defaults apply).",
          "Direction lives in component class names. In the classic new-york-v4 sources the scan counts 121 physical utilities (ml-, pr-, left-…) against 5 logical ones (ms-, pe-, start-…); the newer registry bases add rtl: variants and a DirectionProvider wrapper (ui/direction.tsx) — 46 lines mention rtl across all scanned sources.",
          "Density is expressed as style presets rather than a mode. Default button height / label text per preset: new-york-v4 36px / 14px on 20px; luma 36px / 14px on 20px; lyra 32px / 12px on 16px; maia 36px / 14px on 20px; mira 28px / 12px on 19.5px; nova 32px / 14px on 20px; rhea 32px / 14px on 20px; sera 40px / 12px on 16px; vega 36px / 14px on 20px.",
          "Inputs use 16px text below the md breakpoint and 14px above (avoids iOS zoom) at an unchanged 36px height."
        ]
